# Deploy the mischief Worker to ratstack.sh from the single Stack

## Step

Replace the placeholder R2 bucket in `apps/infra/alchemy.run.ts` with the `Mischief` Worker, `domain: "ratstack.sh"`, plus any DNS records the not-applicable step decided. Confirm with Joel, then `pnpm infra:deploy`, curl `/`, `/llms.txt`, `/mcp` (initialize), and record the URL and the Stack output. Add `pnpm mischief:smoke` that does the curls and runs the isitagentready scan API, printing the level.

Resolved when `https://ratstack.sh/` answers with the agent-first page over TLS and the smoke script prints a level.

## Result (2026-09-21), v0

Joel: "ship v0". Deployed the committed prototype (`01d07df` plus this step's infra change) from a clean rift of `main`, stage `prod`, Alchemy profile `default`, state in `Cloudflare.state()` (already bootstrapped). Plan: 1 create (Mischief), 1 adopt (RatstackZone). Deploy: 9.1 s. Stack output `{ mischiefUrl: 'https://ratstack.sh' }`. Worker name `ratstack-mischief-prod-…`. The placeholder R2 bucket is gone; `alchemy dev` still skips the zone.

Verified live over TLS: `/` 200 `text/markdown`; `Accept: text/html` gets the shell with `<title>`, `og:image`, `<pre>`; `/llms.txt` 200; `/robots.txt` 200; `/nope` 404; `www.ratstack.sh` 301 to the apex. MCP on `2026-07-28`: `server/discover` returns the server card with `supportedVersions: ["2026-07-28"]`, `resources/list` shows `ratstack://repo/AGENTS.md`. A pre-2026 `initialize` without the version header gets 400 "MCP-Protocol-Version header is required", which is the honest answer until the legacy-sessions decision.

Second deploy in the same session: `/og.png` was 404 because the prototype never wired `apps/mischief/public`; added `assets: { directory: "../mischief/public" }` (cwd-relative to `apps/infra`, the Alchemy convention), 3 assets uploaded, all three images 200.

Still open on this step: `pnpm mischief:smoke` (the curls plus the isitagentready scan printing the level). The tools, catalogue, skills, and well-known documents are v0.1, in [build-mischief-tools](./build-mischief-tools.svx).

First live scan (`POST https://isitagentready.com/api/scan`, format `agent`), same day: **0/5**. Expected for v0: Level 1 needs two of `robotsTxt`, `sitemap`, `linkHeaders`, and v0 has only robots. Everything the scan lists (sitemap, Link headers, API catalog, MCP server card, agent-skills index, DNS-AID, the auth trio, A2A) is either in [build-mischief-tools](./build-mischief-tools.svx) or the two remaining decisions.

## Result (2026-09-22), v0.1

Joel: "push, I'm on paid already, that's totally fine." Deployed `a617aac` from the shared tree, stage `prod`: plan 1 update plus the new `Mischief/CODE_SANDBOX` WorkerLoader binding, 7.7 s, zone no-op. The account accepted the binding.

Verified live: `/`, `/skills`, `/skills/add-a-capability`, `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`, `/sitemap.xml`, `/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json`, `/.well-known/api-catalog` (`application/linkset+json`), `/.well-known/mcp.json`, `/openapi.json`, `/og.png` all 200 with the right content types; the root carries the Link header (api-catalog, service-desc, describedby, alternate). MCP `tools/list` on `2026-07-28` returns `search`, `read`, `execute`. A live `execute` program called `search` then `read` inside a fresh Dynamic Worker and returned `ratstack://skills/add-a-capability` with the skill's head; a program calling `fetch` got "This worker is not permitted to access the internet via global functions", so `globalOutbound: null` holds in production.

Live scan the same hour: **4/5, Agent-Integrated**, up from 0/5 on v0. Remaining findings are exactly the Level 5 groups and the not-applicable set: DNS-AID, OAuth discovery, OAuth protected resource, `auth.md`, A2A card, WebMCP, ARD manifest.

Still open: `pnpm mischief:smoke`; the `execute` tool's argument is `code`, worth saying in the tool description since the first guess was `program`.
